# Every app builds from the monorepo root, so anything left here is uploaded to
# the builder on every deploy of every app. The entries below were ~91 MB of a
# ~108 MB context and are used by none of the images.

# Trigger.dev's LOCAL build cache, created by `npm run trigger:dev`. Not tracked
# in git, so it only exists on developer machines — which is why CI never saw
# the cost. Workflows deploy via `trigger.dev deploy`, never from this dir.
packages/tasks/.trigger

# The Astro marketing site builds from its OWN context (CI runs flyctl with
# working-directory: apps/site, so apps/site/.dockerignore applies there, not
# this file). Nothing built from the repo root serves it.
#
# Only the blog content is dropped, not the whole directory: apps/site is a
# workspace in the root package.json, and removing its package.json would break
# `npm ci`'s workspace resolution for every image.
apps/site/src/content

# Playwright fixtures (including a 4.6 MB import .zip). Tests run against a
# live dev stack, never inside an image.
**/tests
**/playwright.config.ts
